      "body": "## Overview\n\nFollow-up to #62561: fill the remaining gaps in the B300 part of **Dynamo disaggregated serving on B300 and GB300** for the [SemiAnalysisAI/InferenceX#4231](https://github.com/SemiAnalysisAI/InferenceX/pull/4231) lane ([run 39112710364](https://github.com/SemiAnalysisAI/InferenceX/actions/runs/39112710364)). Guide text only in `recipes/models/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash.yaml`; the command builder output does not change (B300 builder overrides were intentionally left out in #62561).\n\n## Claims\n\n- **Co-located prefill engines:** up to four DEP2 prefill engines share a B300 node. Add the per-engine `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`, `VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_PORT`, KV-event port (`--kv-events-config` endpoint and the sidecar's `DYN_VLLM_KV_EVENT_PORT`) and `--data-parallel-rpc-port`, plus `VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_HOST` (it defaults to localhost, which breaks cross-node NIXL).\n- **EFA prerequisite:** name the installer the lane used (aws-efa-installer 1.50.0, Ubuntu 24.04 debs plus `libhwloc15`), give an `ldd` check for NIXL's LIBFABRIC plugin, and say to expose `/dev/infiniband` to the container.\n- **Decode graphs:** the c2048 point steps by 24 above 480 (to 792), not 6.\n- **Frontend:** name the `X-Dynamo-Session-Id` header that carries the conversation ID.\n- **PD layout note:** the generic \"TP8 per role on 8-GPU nodes\" sentence now points to the DEP lanes.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Values come from the run's engine/sidecar launch lines and env (per-engine GPUs, side-channel and KV-event ports, DP RPC ports) and the lane's setup script.\n- `node scripts/validate-source.mjs --source vllm --dir <this checkout>/recipes` in vllm-project/recipes passes; `git diff --check` is clean.\n- Rendered every hardware x strategy x feature selection before and after: no change. Merges cleanly with #62541 (same file).\n\n## Details\n\nExcluded as InferenceX harness only: synthetic acceptance, AIPerf/trace replay, Slurm, telemetry and health checks.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
