    {
      "additions": 26,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/cbf54dbf567549ea04ff0e358a329f887cf26779/recipes%2Fmodels%2Fdeepseek-ai%2FDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash.yaml",
      "changes": 30,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/recipes%2Fmodels%2Fdeepseek-ai%2FDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash.yaml?ref=cbf54dbf567549ea04ff0e358a329f887cf26779",
      "deletions": 4,
      "filename": "recipes/models/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash.yaml",
      "patch": "@@ -616,7 +616,8 @@ guide: |\n   fronted by `vllm-router --vllm-pd-disaggregation`. Both pools disable FlashInfer\n   autotune plus JIT and CuTeDSL warmup via `--kernel-config`, skip the DeepGEMM warmup\n   (`VLLM_DEEP_GEMM_WARMUP=skip`), and cap `--max-num-seqs` at 32. On 8-GPU nodes the\n-  same layout becomes TP8 per role.\n+  same layout becomes TP8 per role. The tuned B300 and GB300 AgentX lanes use DEP for both\n+  roles instead; see **Dynamo disaggregated serving on B300 and GB300**.\n \n   With **Speculative decoding** on, DSpark runs in both pools so the transferred KV\n   stays compatible.\n@@ -982,7 +983,13 @@ guide: |\n \n   On B300, set `--cpu-distributed-timeout-seconds 7200` for the Engram load. NIXL's\n   LIBFABRIC plugin also needs libfabric and rdma-core from the AWS EFA installer and the\n-  CUDA 12 runtime (`nvidia-cuda-runtime-cu12`), which the image lacks.\n+  CUDA 12 runtime (`nvidia-cuda-runtime-cu12`), which the image lacks. The lane installs the\n+  rdma-core and libfabric packages from\n+  [aws-efa-installer 1.50.0](https://efa-installer.amazonaws.com/aws-efa-installer-1.50.0.tar.gz)\n+  (Ubuntu 24.04 debs, plus `libhwloc15`) inside the container. Check the plugin with\n+  `ldd $(find / -name libplugin_LIBFABRIC.so 2>/dev/null | head -1) | grep \"not found\"`,\n+  which should print nothing, and expose the host's EFA devices (`/dev/infiniband`) to the\n+  container.\n \n   Prefill runs `--data-parallel-size 2` per GPU pair with `--max-num-seqs 64`,\n   `--long-prefill-token-threshold 8192` and `--prefix-cache-retention-interval 32768`. Its\n@@ -997,16 +1004,31 @@ guide: |\n   Prefill graphs:\n   `{\"mode\":\"VLLM_COMPILE\",\"cudagraph_mode\":\"FULL_AND_PIECEWISE\",\"cudagraph_capture_sizes\":[6,12,18,24,30,36,48,60,72,96,120,144,192,240,288,384,480,576,768,1020,1536,2046],\"decoder_replay_cudagraph_capture_sizes\":[6,12,18,24,30,36,48,60,72,96,120,144,192,240,288,384,480,576,768,1020,1536,2048],\"max_cudagraph_capture_size\":2046}`.\n \n+  On B300, up to four prefill engines share a node, so give each engine its own GPUs, NIXL\n+  side channel, KV-event port and DP RPC port, and set the side-channel host to the node's\n+  address (it defaults to localhost, which breaks cross-node transfers):\n+\n+  | Engine on the node | `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` | `VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_PORT` | KV events (`--kv-events-config` endpoint and the sidecar's `DYN_VLLM_KV_EVENT_PORT`) | `--data-parallel-rpc-port` |\n+  |---|---|---|---|---|\n+  | Prefill 0 | `0,1` | 5400 | 5200 | 8400 |\n+  | Prefill 1 | `2,3` | 5402 | 5202 | 8401 |\n+  | Prefill 2 | `4,5` | 5404 | 5204 | 8402 |\n+  | Prefill 3 | `6,7` | 5406 | 5206 | 8403 |\n+  | Decode (DEP8) | `0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7` | next free (5408) | none | 8400 |\n+\n+  Set `VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_HOST=<node IP>` on every engine. Side-channel ports step by at\n+  least the DP size, since each DP rank uses its own port.\n+\n   Decode uses the `NixlConnector` entry alone with `\"kv_role\":\"kv_consumer\"` and\n   `--no-enable-prefix-caching`. It sets `--max-num-batched-tokens` to ten times\n   `--max-num-seqs` and captures FULL decode-only graphs in steps of 6 up to six times\n-  `--max-num-seqs`. It balances experts with `--enable-eplb` and\n+  `--max-num-seqs` (the B300 c2048 point steps by 24 above 480, ending at 792). It balances experts with `--enable-eplb` and\n   `--eplb-config '{\"communicator\":\"symm_mem\",\"num_redundant_experts\":16,\"window_size\":1000,\"step_interval\":3000,\"use_async\":true}'`.\n \n   Launch the sidecars as in **Dynamo sidecar serving**, with\n   `--grpc-startup-deadline-secs 3600`. Start the frontend so that every request prefills\n   on a prefill engine and each session stays on one prefill engine's prefix and host KV\n-  cache. On GB300, also set `DYN_ROUTER_DECODE_ACTIVE_REQUEST_WEIGHT=10000000`.\n+  cache. Send the conversation ID in the `X-Dynamo-Session-Id` request header. On GB300, also set `DYN_ROUTER_DECODE_ACTIVE_REQUEST_WEIGHT=10000000`.\n \n   ```bash\n   export DYN_ROUTER_TEMPERATURE=0 DYN_ROUTER_QUEUE_THRESHOLD=None DYN_ROUTER_ACTIVE_REQUEST_EXPIRY_SECS=3600",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/cbf54dbf567549ea04ff0e358a329f887cf26779/recipes%2Fmodels%2Fdeepseek-ai%2FDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash.yaml",
